 and\n\n- $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ is the usual Cartesian $z$-coordinate.\n\nThe picture shows a circular cylinder of radius $1$ whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis. \n\nWe note the following:\n\n- Since the distance from any point on our surface to the $z$-axis equals $1,$ we must have $r=1$ for every point on the surface.\n\n- On the other hand, $\\theta $ and $z$ can vary arbitrarily in their respective domains.\n\nTherefore, the equation of the surface in cylindrical polar coordinates is $r=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104204/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eae7e5be-e883-5658-84a0-5de5da567887"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104204"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104209/selection/b22775b0789dddb1d795aa22a4599a71a10b6445b231aae2b497e7e49ece2664" :answer/id #uuid "023eec64-fe2d-5487-afbe-ae173ec174f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta =\\frac{11\\pi }{8}r" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104209/selection/a5450769998bef638d75f628174f313df3dd9b189545dbe6f292b025eca97cf8" :answer/id #uuid "ace650a7-b42a-57dd-bd16-bcaff3e8226a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta =\\frac{11\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104209/selection/e37dc0ab4966224601327c052c76dd99ed876b8e27b2b7225443e80cec23128e" :answer/id #uuid "7dcfdef2-5860-5977-b554-de772e02c737" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\frac{11\\pi }{8}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104209/selection/5e35ea29222797252c5f3eb7217fa389c14482ad24a362cd59ffb20151fe7ff8" :answer/id #uuid "f7f72615-3658-5120-8885-931b455a0000" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=\\frac{11\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104209/selection/521109bb203a3108988bc28cb4b61825640387004cadbe58794cee92f148aa3f" :answer/id #uuid "554df06a-9a49-5917-a0a8-58f10b438fc6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answe