 :question/worked-solution "The position of a point in cylindrical polar coordinates is written as $(r,\\theta ,z),$ where \n\n- $r\\ge 0$ and $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$ are the usual plane polar coordinates, and\n\n- $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ is the usual Cartesian $z$-coordinate.\n\nThe picture shows a plane parallel to the $xy$-plane.\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- Since the $z$-coordinate of any point on our surface equals $-1,$ we must have $z=-1$ for every point on the surface.\n\n- On the other hand, $r$ and $\\theta $ can vary arbitrarily in their respective domains.\n\nTherefore, the equation of the surface in cylindrical polar coordinates is $z=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104213/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eae7e5be-e883-5658-84a0-5de5da567887"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104213"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104223/selection/e3bc01c1a7cc4eaaa3d0fec3c0eb87ff9cb3bf03f2891a742d43b82797869ffc" :answer/id #uuid "d51eaf3e-769f-51e9-be58-884e2f120003" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A circular cylinder" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104223/selection/826bf7aafa9cc6ead7419f848f42490f26708d4b2d9f0ac9dc3dad7483a7dd05" :answer/id #uuid "7c0f9ddf-85d9-556e-9da6-37686ebea0eb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A cone" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104223/selection/c42687c1e0e0b1f1d69a99bb36f784671f2be77b295e7dc563f9366ef570bdd1" :answer/id #uuid "605b2426-91f9-5e77-831c-8975c1f7853a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A half-cone" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104223/selection/9a01d3b7bb50f74f0f0a937ec21e923b3fd4baedfed010beb5720f21b3f20cd5" :answer/id #uuid "5b105edc-895d-58b0-9bc1-509adde9dd79" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A half-plane that passes through the $z$-axis" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104223/selection/bb8c34e3a8d482c4f322d1